    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nDNS (Domain Name System) translates domain names to IP addresses. It is a hierarchical, distributed database. Query flow: browser -> cache -> recursive resolver -> root -> TLD -> authoritative nameserver. Key points to remember: - Recursive resolver: does the legwork. - Root: points to TLD servers. - TLD:.com,.org, etc. - Authoritative: holds the actual DNS record. A strong interview answer should connect the definition to how the concept works internally, its important trade-offs, and one realistic use case. The goal is not only to name the concept but to explain why and when it is useful.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks whether you can explain DNS and how does it accurately and connect the definition to a practical consequence. A strong answer should also acknowledge the main limitation or boundary.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. DNS (Domain Name System) translates domain names to IP addresses.\n2. It is a hierarchical, distributed database.\n3. Query flow: browser -> cache -> recursive resolver -> root -> TLD -> authoritative nameserver.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nI would define it first, explain the part that actually changes the outcome, and use the example to show I understand it in practice.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in a production application, a team can apply this concept to a concrete requirement and verify the behavior described in the answer. DNS (Domain Name System) translates domain names to IP addresses.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn a production application, engineers use this when they need the behavior described by the question. DNS (Domain Name System) translates domain names to IP addresses.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Stopping at the definition without explaining how the concept behaves.\n- Using an example that does not actually demonstrate the point.\n- Making an absolute claim when configuration, version, workload, or context changes the result.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nStay close to the exact question. One technically precise example is more valuable than a broad overview of the entire technology.",
