    shortDescription: "Compare the two.",
    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nZuul 1.x is blocking, based on servlet. Spring Cloud Gateway is non-blocking, based on Spring WebFlux and Reactor, offering better performance and modern features. Spring Cloud Gateway is preferred for new projects.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThe interviewer is checking whether you can explain the boundary between the two choices in what is the difference between zuul and spring cloud gateway and tie that difference to an engineering decision.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Zuul 1.x is blocking, based on servlet.\n2. Spring Cloud Gateway is non-blocking, based on Spring WebFlux and Reactor, offering better performance and modern features.\n3. Spring Cloud Gateway is preferred for new projects.\n4. Distinguish language/runtime guarantees from framework conventions and call out version-sensitive behavior when it changes the answer..\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nDefine both sides briefly, state the real boundary between them, and then give the condition that would make you choose one over the other.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in a Spring Boot service, choose the option whose behavior matches the requirement and compare the resulting operational consequence. Zuul 1.x is blocking, based on servlet.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn a Spring Boot service, engineers use this when they need the behavior described by the question. Zuul 1.x is blocking, based on servlet.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Defining both sides but never stating the practical difference.\n- Choosing one option without naming the requirement that drives the choice.\n- Treating platform-specific behavior as a universal rule.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nState the decision rule early: when would you choose A, and when would you choose B? That is more useful than listing every secondary difference.",
