    question: "How does InnoDB implement row-level locking?",
    slug: "innodb-row-locking",
    shortDescription: "Explain MVCC and locking.",
    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nInnoDB uses multi-version concurrency control (MVCC) for non-locking reads. For writes, it uses row-level locks (shared/exclusive) on index entries. It also supports gap locks and next-key locks to prevent phantom reads.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks whether you can explain InnoDB implement row-level locking accurately and connect the definition to a practical consequence. A strong answer should also acknowledge the main limitation or boundary.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. InnoDB uses multi-version concurrency control (MVCC) for non-locking reads.\n2. For writes, it uses row-level locks (shared/exclusive) on index entries.\n3. It also supports gap locks and next-key locks to prevent phantom reads.\n4. Tie the explanation to data shape, access pattern, concurrency, and the evidence you would use to judge performance or correctness..\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nStart with the answer in one sentence, then explain the mechanism that makes it true. Give one concrete example and stop before drifting into unrelated details.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in a production application, a team can apply this concept to a concrete requirement and verify the behavior described in the answer. InnoDB uses multi-version concurrency control (MVCC) for non-locking reads.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn a production application, engineers use this when they need the behavior described by the question. InnoDB uses multi-version concurrency control (MVCC) for non-locking reads.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Assuming a schema or index is automatically faster without checking access patterns.\n- Ignoring concurrency or consistency requirements.\n- Quoting performance characteristics without measured evidence.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nStay close to the exact question. One technically precise example is more valuable than a broad overview of the entire technology.",
